Sareeha.

c0951
00:33:45.000 --> 00:33:46.000
No and yes.

c0952
00:33:46.000 --> 00:33:47.000
I'm sorry.

c0953
00:33:47.000 --> 00:33:48.000
Yes.

c0954
00:33:48.000 --> 00:33:49.000
Very important.

c0955
00:33:49.000 --> 00:33:50.000
First of all,

c0956
00:33:50.000 --> 00:33:51.000
that's a very important thing.

c0957
00:33:51.000 --> 00:33:54.000
At the end of the 40 years,

c0958
00:33:54.000 --> 00:33:57.000
because Moshe Rabbenu wrote the Tora

c0959
00:33:57.000 --> 00:34:00.000
at the end of 40 years in the desert.

c0960
00:34:00.000 --> 00:34:03.000
When he writes the Tora,

c0961
00:34:03.000 --> 00:34:06.000
he writes 13 copies of the Tora,

c0962
00:34:06.000 --> 00:34:08.000
Moshe Rabbenu.

c0963
00:34:08.000 --> 00:34:10.000
And the way it goes is as follows.

c0964
00:34:11.000 --> 00:34:15.000
It gives one copy of the Sefer Tora

c0965
00:34:15.000 --> 00:34:17.000
to each tribe.

c0966
00:34:17.000 --> 00:34:20.000
And one copy,

c0967
00:34:20.000 --> 00:34:24.000
he puts in the Aron Ha'idut.

c0968
00:34:24.000 --> 00:34:26.000
In that Aron Ha'idut,

c0969
00:34:26.000 --> 00:34:28.000
he leaves it there.

c0970
00:34:28.000 --> 00:34:29.000
You see?

c0971
00:34:29.000 --> 00:34:30.000
And therefore,

c0972
00:34:30.000 --> 00:34:31.000
why this is so important?

c0973
00:34:31.000 --> 00:34:32.000
Why this?

c0974
00:34:32.000 --> 00:34:33.000
Because like this.

c0975
00:34:33.000 --> 00:34:34.000
Suppose, I don't know,

c0976
00:34:34.000 --> 00:34:37.000
a thousand years later,

c0977
00:34:38.000 --> 00:34:41.000
U'bevo Moshe la'Qodesh.

c0978
00:34:41.000 --> 00:34:42.000
So, I say,

c0979
00:34:42.000 --> 00:34:46.000
it has to be with a Bab.

c0980
00:34:46.000 --> 00:34:49.000
No, it doesn't have to be with a Bab.

c0981
00:34:49.000 --> 00:34:52.000
How do you know how to write it?

c0982
00:34:52.000 --> 00:34:56.000
There's only one way how do you do it.

c0983
00:34:56.000 --> 00:35:00.000
You go to the Bet ha-Miqdash,

c0984
00:35:00.000 --> 00:35:03.000
and then you check it

c0985
00:35:03.000 --> 00:35:04.000
against the original.

c0986
00:35:04.000 --> 00:35:05.000
That is the original.

c0987
00:35:05.000 --> 00:35:06.000
And therefore,

c0988
00:35:06.000 --> 00:35:09.000
this original serves to validate

c0989
00:35:09.000 --> 00:35:11.000
all future copies.

c0990
00:35:11.000 --> 00:35:13.000
Do you understand?

c0991
00:35:13.000 --> 00:35:14.000
Ultimately,

c0992
00:35:14.000 --> 00:35:16.000
sometimes there's a voice with a Bab.

c0993
00:35:16.000 --> 00:35:18.000
Sometimes it's without a Bab.

c0994
00:35:20.000 --> 00:35:21.000
You could argue with me,

c0995
00:35:21.000 --> 00:35:22.000
I could argue with Bab.

c0996
00:35:22.000 --> 00:35:24.000
How could we prove it?

c0997
00:35:24.000 --> 00:35:25.000
Ultimately,

c0998
00:35:25.000 --> 00:35:27.000
there's only one way to do it.

c0999
00:35:27.000 --> 00:35:28.000
We validate.

c1000
00:35:28.000 --> 00:35:30.000
Now, out of this

c1001
00:35:30.000 --> 00:35:32.000
came a very important Sepharadi custom.

c1002
00:35:32.000 --> 00:35:33.000
You will not believe it,

c1003
00:35:33.000 --> 00:35:35.000
but only the Sephardim have discussed it.

c1004
00:35:35.000 --> 00:35:36.000
Not only Sephardim,

c1005
00:35:36.000 --> 00:35:37.000
also Temanim.

c1006
00:35:37.000 --> 00:35:40.000
Sephardim and Oriental Jews in the Orient,

c1007
00:35:40.000 --> 00:35:41.000
like the Yemenites,

c1008
00:35:41.000 --> 00:35:42.000
they have it.

c1009
00:35:42.000 --> 00:35:43.000
We had,

c1010
00:35:43.000 --> 00:35:44.000
for instance,

c1011
00:35:44.000 --> 00:35:45.000
Halab was famous for this.

c1012
00:35:45.000 --> 00:35:46.000
Sham also was famous for this.

c1013
00:35:46.000 --> 00:35:48.000
Egypt was famous for this.

c1014
00:35:48.000 --> 00:35:51.000
Each community had a Taj.

c1015
00:35:51.000 --> 00:35:54.000
You know what Taj is?

c1016
00:35:54.000 --> 00:35:56.000
The word Taj means a crown.

c1017
00:35:56.000 --> 00:35:58.000
But it was not a crown.

c1018
00:35:58.000 --> 00:36:02.000
It was a manuscript Sefer Tora.

c1019
00:36:03.000 --> 00:36:05.000
The oldest and most authoritative things

c1020
00:36:05.000 --> 00:36:07.000
that was kept

c1021
00:36:07.000 --> 00:36:10.000
in the archives of the community.

c1022
00:36:10.000 --> 00:36:12.000
And therefore,

c1023
00:36:12.000 --> 00:36:14.000
whenever there's a problem in the Sefer Tora,

c1024
00:36:14.000 --> 00:36:15.000
it should be written this way,

c1025
00:36:15.000 --> 00:36:17.000
not should be written this way.

c1026
00:36:17.000 --> 00:36:19.000
They used to go

c1027
00:36:19.000 --> 00:36:21.000
and check it

c1028
00:36:21.000 --> 00:36:24.000
against this Taj.

c1029
00:36:24.000 --> 00:36:25.000
You understand?

c1030
00:36:25.000 --> 00:36:27.000
And thereby they determine

c1031
00:36:27.000 --> 00:36:30.000
whether it is a kosher or unkosher Sefer Tora.

c1032
00:36:30.000 --> 00:36:33.000
Every single Sepharadi community

c1033
00:36:33.000 --> 00:36:35.000
throughout history

c1034
00:36:35.000 --> 00:36:36.000
up to the modern times,

c1035
00:36:36.000 --> 00:36:40.000
the most famous Taj of all

c1036
00:36:40.000 --> 00:36:42.000
is the Taj of Aramsoba,

c1037
00:36:42.000 --> 00:36:43.000
of Halab.

c1038
00:36:43.000 --> 00:36:44.000
Why?

c1039
00:36:44.000 --> 00:36:48.000
Because it belonged to Rambam.

c1040
00:36:48.000 --> 00:36:50.000
And what happened to it,

c1041
00:36:50.000 --> 00:36:55.000
part of it was burnt or destroyed.

c1042
00:36:55.000 --> 00:36:59.000
The greatest modern lie

c1043
00:36:59.000 --> 00:37:01.000
is about the Arabs.

c1044
00:37:01.000 --> 00:37:04.000
The Arabs are wild animals

c1045
00:37:04.000 --> 00:37:06.000
that have no concept,

c1046
00:37:06.000 --> 00:37:07.000
no respect for religion,

c1047
00:37:07.000 --> 00:37:09.000
no respect for nothing.

c1048
00:37:09.000 --> 00:37:11.000
About 20, 30 years ago,

c1049
00:37:11.000 --> 00:37:14.000
1948, I think,

c1050
00:37:14.000 --> 00:37:15.000
1947,

c1051
00:37:15.000 --> 00:37:16.000
yeah,

c1052
00:37:16.000 --> 00:37:19.000
they went into the Knesset of Aramsoba.

c1053
00:37:19.000 --> 00:37:22.000
And what they wanted to do in the Knesset?

c1054
00:37:22.000 --> 00:37:25.000
They burnt part of the Taj.

c1055
00:37:25.000 --> 00:37:27.000
You have to be animals.

c1056
00:37:27.000 --> 00:37:29.000
You have to be an animal to this.

c1057
00:37:29.000 --> 00:37:31.000
Why you burnt the Sefer Tora?

c1058
00:37:31.000 --> 00:37:33.000
Why is it?

c1059
00:37:33.000 --> 00:37:35.000
But part of it,

c1060
00:37:35.000 --> 00:37:37.000
two-thirds of it,

c1061
00:37:37.000 --> 00:37:38.000
is intact,

c1062
00:37:38.000 --> 00:37:41.000
and it is in exhibit in Jerusalem.

c1063
00:37:41.000 --> 00:37:43.000
When you go to Jerusalem,

c1064
00:37:43.000 --> 00:37:45.000
they have Hecharas Sefer.

c1065
00:37:45.000 --> 00:37:46.000
You go to Hecharas Sefer,

c1066
00:37:46.000 --> 00:37:48.000
and it is exhibited

c1067
00:37:48.000 --> 00:37:52.000
among the most precious treasures

